              "text": "ಗಂಡ (gaṇḍa) — \"husband\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The everyday word, and a native one. Its own stem also gives ಗಂಡು (gaṇḍu), 'male', so what it names is a man of the house rather than anything about the wedding. Formal Kannada keeps the Sanskrit pati alongside it for writing and ceremony."
            }
          ]
        },
